  "question": "Let $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$ be such that $\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}=0$ and $|\\vec{a}+\\vec{b}| = |\\vec{a}| = 5$, $|\\vec{b}|=c$. Find $c$.",
  "answeroption": "C",
  "explanation": "$|\\vec{a}+\\vec{b}|^2 = |\\vec{a}|^2 + 2 \\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b} + |\\vec{b}|^2$.<br /><br />Since $\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b}=0$, we get $|\\vec{a}+\\vec{b}|^2 = 25 + c^2$.<br /><br />But $|\\vec{a}+\\vec{b}| = 5$.<br /><br />So $25 = 25 + c^2 \\Rightarrow c^2 = 0$.<br /><br />Thus $c=0$.",
